      "body": "## Motivation\n\naiter mHC pre/post is gated to gfx95. On gfx942 (MI300X / MI325X) the fused mHC post/pre boundary therefore selects `mhc_fused_post_pre`, whose TileLang kernel uses `tl.get_lane_idx()`. TileLang's HIP codegen cannot lower that op on gfx942, so CUDA-graph capture dies with:\n\n```\ntvm.error.InternalError: Unresolved call Op(tl.get_lane_idx)\nException: Capture cuda graph failed: Unresolved call Op(tl.get_lane_idx)\n```\n\naiter's mHC kernels do run on gfx942 with their default config for that CU count. Using them, instead of the unfused torch fallback, is what made GLM-5.3-Flash decode on MI300X fast enough for RL rollout.\n\n#41136 avoids the TileLang crash by turning the fused boundary off for all HIP. This PR takes the other route on gfx942: run aiter, and only skip the TileLang kernel that cannot compile there. gfx95 and gfx1250 are unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `_use_aiter_mhc()` and `_is_aiter_gfx95_mhc_available()` also accept gfx942, so pre, post, and `mhc_fused_post_pre` use aiter when `SGLANG_USE_AITER=1`.\n- `_is_fused_mhc_post_pre_enabled()` returns false on gfx942, after the gfx1250 early return, so the TileLang fused kernel is never chosen there.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMI300X, GLM-5.3-Flash BF16, TP8, aiter mHC, decode CUDA graphs. The server completes graph capture and serves. Teacher-forced logprobs against the trainer, after the separate routing-bias fix, match the previous rollout build (`train_rollout_logprob_abs_diff` 0.06–0.09 over 4 RL steps). With routing replay the gap was 0.022–0.029.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nDecode throughput, 512 output tokens per request, TP8, one MI300X node:\n\n| Concurrency | Previous build, torch mHC | This branch, aiter mHC |\n|---|---|---|\n| 16 | 945 tok/s | 1031 tok/s |\n| 64 | 1914 tok/s | 2349 tok/s |\n| 128 | — | 3000 tok/s |\n\nAt concurrency 128 the GPU spends about 35 ms per decode step. The pure-torch mHC fallback had been the largest CPU-side cost in the previous build (about 46% of scheduler samples).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38937330848](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38937330848)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38937330755](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38937330755)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38937330795](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38937330795)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
